From b30e97472662e2edc751aa8e82a29a5187fd13fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:22:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Close REFRESH-006: add real mid-flight cancellation for
 refresh/live jobs

Add CancelToken/RefreshCancelled to ausl_data.py and thread cancel_token
through _fetch_with_retry, _get_json, _get_text, _download_file,
fetch_standings_frame, fetch_schedule_frame, update_all_data, and
fetch_live_game. Cancellation is checked before each network attempt and
during the retry backoff wait (via Event.wait instead of time.sleep), so a
cancelled job stops retrying immediately instead of working through its
full timeout/retry budget. update_all_data also re-checks cancellation
right before staging/promotion so a cancelled Quick Refresh can never write
or promote a partial result.

In ausl_stats_app.py, add cancel_data_update()/cancel_live_refresh() plus
Cancel buttons, wire game changes and app shutdown to cancel an in-flight
live/refresh job, and give each job a per-call CancelToken/token-identity
check so a late success/error/cancelled callback from an abandoned
background thread is a safe no-op instead of promoting stale data or
crashing. Idempotent: repeated cancel calls and a cancel racing a
just-completed success/failure are all handled safely.

Existing test doubles for _get_json/_get_text/fetch_standings_frame/
fetch_schedule_frame/update_all_data/fetch_live_game are updated to accept
the new optional cancel_token parameter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
